# Prospective selection and percentile dispatch candidate

The frozen two-module candidate regressed the fixed organ-pipe p95 timing by 27.91056% versus the unchanged baseline. This separate stage tests a different pivot/work strategy and less repeated work in multi-percentile dispatch. The old measured study, inputs, thresholds, raw logs and production remain unchanged.

Before implementation, the planned finite-number path is a private single-pass candidate copy, a median of nine evenly spaced samples for sufficiently large partitions, then deterministic groups-of-five median selection once cumulative partition scans exceed twice the initial length. All comparison/partition work has an explicit conservative `64*n+128` charge limit. Exhaustion returns to the existing stable sort with a preserved permutation. A deliberately smaller explicit limit will exercise this refusal contract in correctness tests. These constants are prospective structural limits, not selected from a new performance trial. A worst-case machine-time or linear-time guarantee is not claimed.

Null filtering remains strict-null filtering for percentile reducers; undefined, sparse holes, nonfinite values, signed zero and coercible primitives retain the authentic stable sort behavior. Finite fast-path collection may avoid the old duplicate filter/slice arrays, but it must never change caller values or cache/alias behavior.

Multi-percentile requests continue to share one complete stable sort. Their selected results will be assigned directly at each original queue position, avoiding a temporary one-property result and repeated special-reducer dispatch. The standard reducer and all non-percentile special bodies remain exact. Sparse multiselection is deliberately not added to this stage.

Acceptance will replay the complete 2,910,751 original reducer comparisons (including 48,240 cache checks) plus 14,240 standard helper checks, held-out selection and standard/coercion cases, the exact previous 42-input corpus, all fixed seven measured input shapes, additional deterministic adversarial inputs and explicit budget-exhaustion/permutation/cache controls. Both candidate modules and all actual original CJS/Lodash authorities will be authenticated before/after every run; failures and actual executed sources are retained.

This is correctness-only preparation. No timing, memory measurement, profiling, integration or superiority claim is authorized. Source-layout effects and possible small-array overhead remain unresolved until a future separately authorized quiet interval.
